<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria M1 rises 6.66 pct, M2 up 4.78 pct in week.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria M1 rises 6.66 pct, M2 up 4.78 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian M1 money supply rose to 618.5 billion levs on May 2 from 579.9 billion levs a week earlier and M2 edged up to 3,119 billion levs from 2,976.6 billion levs, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Total broad money rose 5.1 percent to 3,298.6 billion levs in the week to May 2.</p>
<p>Conversion of dollar-denominated deposits into levs was made at the central bank fixings of 1,492.8 levs per dollar for May 2, 1,467.8 for April 25 and 1,590.8 for March 28.</p>
